+    <section class="card span-4" id="data-notes">
+      <h2>Data Notes (for analysts)</h2>
+      <ul class="small">
+        <li>Frequency: weekly; retail prices are USD/L; Brent is USD/bbl.</li>
+        <li>Brent is global (shared value per week); retail prices vary by country.</li>
+        <li><code>tax_percentage</code> varies week-to-week within countries (estimation/measurement variability in source).</li>
+        <li>Subsidy regime in data includes <code>Low</code>, <code>Medium</code>, <code>High</code>, <code>Very High</code>.</li>
+      </ul>
+      <div class="note-box">
+        Limitations: no explicit volumes/consumption weights are provided, so all "global" averages are unweighted across observations.
+      </div>
+    </section>
+
+    <section class="card span-12" id="temporal-trends">
+      <h2>Temporal Price Trends & Volatility</h2>
+      <p class="small">
+        Global weekly means show tight co-movement with Brent over 2020–2026 (petrol r={_fmt_num(corr_petrol,4)}, diesel r={_fmt_num(corr_diesel,4)}).
+        Volatility (std. dev. of weekly % changes): Brent {_fmt_num(metrics['volatility']['brent_weekly_pct_std']*100,2)}pp, petrol {_fmt_num(metrics['volatility']['petrol_weekly_pct_std']*100,2)}pp, diesel {_fmt_num(metrics['volatility']['diesel_weekly_pct_std']*100,2)}pp.
+      </p>
+      <canvas id="chart_trends"></canvas>
+      <div class="note-box">
+        Retail petrol weekly-mean extremes: low on <b>{pet_min['date']}</b> ({_fmt_num(pet_min['value'], 3)} USD/L) and high on <b>{pet_max['date']}</b> ({_fmt_num(pet_max['value'], 3)} USD/L).
+      </div>
+      <div style="margin-top:10px" class="small">
+        <b>Largest absolute weekly Brent moves (top 10)</b>
+      </div>
+      <table class="table">
+        <thead><tr><th>Date</th><th>Weekly % change</th><th>Abs. % change</th></tr></thead>
+        <tbody>
+          {''.join([f"<tr><td>{m['date']}</td><td>{_fmt_pct(m['pct_change'],1)}</td><td>{_fmt_pct(m['abs_pct_change'],1)}</td></tr>" for m in metrics['top_brent_weekly_moves']])}
+        </tbody>
+      </table>
+    </section>
+
+    <section class="card span-12" id="regional-comparison">
+      <h2>Regional Price Disparities</h2>
+      <p class="small">
+        Regional averages (petrol) highlight persistent price inequality. The annual regional spread (max–min regional average petrol) ranges from
+        {_fmt_num(min(metrics['regional_spread_yearly'].values()), 3)} USD/L to {_fmt_num(max(metrics['regional_spread_yearly'].values()), 3)} USD/L across 2020–2026.
+      </p>
+      <canvas id="chart_region_year"></canvas>
+      <canvas id="chart_spread"></canvas>
+    </section>
+
+    <section class="card span-12" id="subsidy-tax-analysis">
