+      </div>
+      <canvas id="chart_subsidy_trends"></canvas>
+      <div style="margin-top:10px" class="small">
+        <b>Income segmentation (High vs Low subsidy)</b>: average petrol prices by income level and subsidy label.
+      </div>
+      <canvas id="chart_income_subsidy"></canvas>
+      <div class="note-box">
+        Dampening within income groups (High vs Low subsidy label):
+        {', '.join([f"<b>{html.escape(inc)}</b>={_fmt_num(p,1)}%" for inc,p in metrics['dampening_by_income'].items()])}.
+      </div>
+    </section>
+
+    <section class="card span-6" id="income-level-segmentation">
+      <h2>Fuel Affordability by Income Level</h2>
+      <p class="small">
+        The dataset’s <code>tax_percentage</code> indicates higher average fuel-tax shares in High-income observations.
+        This interacts with the level of subsidy support to shape both affordability and fiscal exposure.
+      </p>
+      <canvas id="chart_tax_income"></canvas>
+      <div class="note-box">
+        Tax-to-price ratio (avg %): High {_fmt_num(tax_high,1)}%, Middle {_fmt_num(tax_mid,1)}%, Low {_fmt_num(tax_low,1)}%.
+      </div>
+    </section>
+
+    <section class="card span-6" id="key-findings-recommendations">
